-- §16  How much of each contract the difference guarding it is actually about.
# One row per contract: its subjects, how many the population answered, the shortfall, and a
# verdict.
#
# §15's reading, one level up
#   There a zero is a layer a relation does not reach; here it is a subject the population never
#   reached, so the only thing putting it on the produced side is the roster the produced side is
#   being compared against.
#
# This and reports/coverage.sqlc move in opposite directions
#   They move oppositely on one event. On the `rules` row, the subjects short are the rules
#   coverage calls `VACUOUS`, by construction rather than by coincidence: both read
#   `violates IS NOT NULL` over checks/all.sqlc. So a filing that gives one of them rows improves
#   coverage and takes a subject away from here, in one event. Neither table says that alone, and
#   that is why the pair is printed.
#
# `ok` is not one fact
#   A contract whose population the contract did not write earns it; so does one built exactly like
#   `rules` whose population merely happens to be complete. The two are a template apart, and a
#   query cannot tell them apart at all, which is why `examples/soundness` checks it beside this
#   and not inside it.
#
# It grades a worked-out column
#   It grades a worked-out column rather than restricting one, which is a weaker thing than §15
#   does. `subjects - witnessed` is arithmetic over rank/guard_reach.sqlc's own counts, and the
#   verdict is a rendering, so nothing here is a second opinion about anything.
-- rank/guard_reach.sqlc, with the shortfall worked out and named.
SELECT c.contract                                  AS "contract!",
       c.subjects                                  AS "subjects!",
       c.witnessed                                 AS "witnessed!",
       c.subjects - c.witnessed                    AS "roster_only!",
       CASE WHEN c.subjects = c.witnessed THEN 'ok'
            ELSE 'the roster puts these on both sides of the difference'
       END                                         AS "verdict!"
FROM (
    :compose(rank/guard_reach.sqlc)
) c
ORDER BY c.subjects - c.witnessed DESC, c.contract
